From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Heider <tobias.heider@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Feb 2025 16:34:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on Acer
 Swift 14 models

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2100858

Add the aforementioned machines to the list to get e.g. efivars up.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Heider <tobias.heider@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00111
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@65f28d0040bb56914264c9fc9c4e4b99c84f3960
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 3eaa4c9ccf3c..d4d841fb607f 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2300,6 +2300,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_qseecom_app_send);
  + any potential issues with this, only allow validated machines for now.
  */
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
+	{ .compatible = "acer,swift-sf14-11" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
